Security bug reproduction: our homegrown sanitizer below is bypassable. Copy it verbatim into /workspace/fix-sanitizer/src/naive.js, then demonstrate at least three distinct bypasses with failing tests before fixing anything.

export function sanitize(html) {
  return html
    .replace(/<script[^>]*>[\s\S]*?<\/script>/gi, '')
    .replace(/ on\w+="[^"]*"/gi, '')
    .replace(/javascript:/gi, '');
}

Bypass ideas to explore: unquoted or single-quoted event handlers, nested markers that reappear after one removal pass (like jajavascript:vascript:), and non-script vectors such as iframe or img onerror. Write vitest tests asserting the sanitized output of each payload contains no executable vector by parsing with node-html-parser (no on-prefixed attribute anywhere, no script or iframe element, no javascript: scheme after entity decoding). Watch them fail against naive.js, then write src/fixed.js as a parse-and-rebuild allowlist sanitizer that makes the same tests pass. Keep both files; tests import fixed for the green run.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

